
[38;5;25m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[0m
  [1;38;5;25mAAOS SDV + CARLA Quickstart Guide[0m
[38;5;25m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[0m

Welcome! This cloud workstation lets you run a 3D simulated car alongside
[1mAndroid Automotive OS (AAOS)[0m and [1mSoftware-Defined Vehicle (SDV)[0m services
right in your browser.

  [1;38;5;25m•[0m [1;38;5;130mTip for pasting commands:[0m In this Linux terminal, use
    [1mRight-Click -> Paste[0m or [1;38;5;55;48;5;254m[Ctrl+Shift+V][0m.

[38;5;250m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[0m
[1;38;5;25m1. Run the Live Vehicle Simulation (3 Steps)[0m
[38;5;250m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[0m

[1;38;5;255;48;5;25m Step 1a [0m [1;38;5;18mStart the Android virtual machines[0m
Copy and paste this command to boot both virtual machines (takes ~30 seconds):

    [1;38;5;23;48;5;254m  launch_2vm  [0m

[1;38;5;255;48;5;25m Step 1b [0m [1;38;5;18mStart the 3D car simulator (CARLA)[0m
Copy and paste this command to open the 3D driving window and stream live
car signals (speed, gear, RPM) to the Android displays:

    [1;38;5;23;48;5;254m  launch_carla  [0m

[3;38;5;241m(Note: If your workstation does not have CARLA pre-installed yet, run this
once first, then run [0m[1;38;5;23;48;5;254m launch_carla [0m[3;38;5;241m again):[0m

    [1;38;5;23;48;5;254m  install_carla  [0m

[1;38;5;236mDriving controls inside the CARLA car window:[0m
  [1;38;5;25m•[0m Press [1;38;5;55;48;5;254m[p][0m to turn autopilot on or off
  [1;38;5;25m•[0m Use [1;38;5;55;48;5;254m[W][0m, [1;38;5;55;48;5;254m[A][0m, [1;38;5;55;48;5;254m[S][0m, [1;38;5;55;48;5;254m[D][0m keys to drive manually
  [1;38;5;25m•[0m Press [1;38;5;55;48;5;254m[Backspace][0m if autopilot gets stuck
  [1;38;5;25m•[0m Press [1;38;5;55;48;5;254m[?][0m to see all keyboard shortcuts

[1;38;5;255;48;5;25m Step 1c [0m [1;38;5;18mOpen the vehicle displays in Chrome[0m
Copy and paste this command to open the Android displays in a browser window:

    [1;38;5;23;48;5;254m  visualize_cvd  [0m

[1;38;5;236mWhat you will see in Chrome (under "Devices" on the left):[0m
  [1;38;5;25m•[0m [1;38;5;23;48;5;254m vm0 [0m [1m(SDV Instrument Cluster):[0m Shows the driver cluster display.
    Speed, RPM, and gear update live as the car drives in CARLA.
  [1;38;5;25m•[0m [1;38;5;23;48;5;254m vm1 [0m [1m(AAOS IVI Display):[0m Shows the center infotainment screen.

[38;5;250m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[0m
[1;38;5;25m2. Explore and Edit Code in Android Studio (Optional)[0m
[38;5;250m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[0m

Copy and paste this command to open the pre-configured project in
[1mAndroid Studio for Platform (ASfP)[0m:

    [1;38;5;23;48;5;254m  asfp  [0m

[3;38;5;241m(Note: When the project opens, background indexing takes about 2 to 3 minutes
to finish in the bottom-right status bar.)[0m

[38;5;250m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[0m
[1;38;5;25m3. Build and Test with the Antigravity AI Agent (Optional)[0m
[38;5;250m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────[0m

Copy and paste this command to start the [1mAntigravity[0m command-line
assistant in the terminal:

    [1;38;5;23;48;5;254m  antigravity-cli  [0m

